"""A local grammar approximation to this component.

Negation and adverbs after 'be' produce negative pulses, especially
frequency adverbs. Degree words respond less. Past tense strengthens the
pulse; contractions weaken it. The copula cue fades through intervening
modifiers. Smaller rules cover modal negation and causative pronouns.
