"""A negative USE signal: strongest on use, then used/uses, then using.

It also responds more weakly to need, utility vocabulary, and translations
of use. Word boundaries, capitalization, and a few preceding grammatical
words adjust the strength. 'Of' immediately after 'use' carries the signal.
Only the previous token is carried, resetting at document boundaries.
This is a lexical approximation, not a model of general semantic usefulness.
