"""A lexical pair-and-small-group detector.

Pair(s) is strongest; pairing, copies, couples, tuples, coordinates and small
numbered groups are weaker. A few translations of pair/double also respond.
Air-like spellings spill over, especially bare fragments that finish a split
word. The next 'of' inherits 40% of a pair/group response. Other tokens are
zero. This omits the component's many weak lexical responses and most context
variation, rather than storing a large token table.
