"""Negative pulses at comparison/contrast markers, mostly English.

The prepositions in 'different from', 'similar to', 'same as', etc.
respond to a nearby comparison word. 'Than' is weaker after quantities
(more/less/greater) than after qualitative comparatives. 'Unlike' is the
strongest marker, with a smaller echo on a following determiner.
Whole-token Chinese heavenly stems have a separate positive response. Everything else is zero; documents have separate state.
"""
import re

READS = ()
WORDS = re.compile(r'[A-Za-z]+')
# Traditional Chinese year labels, also used to label ordered alternatives.
STEMS = {
    '甲': 4.0, '乙': 3.5, '丙': 3.9, '丁': 6.4, '戊': 5.0,
    '己': 1.3, '庚': 3.9, '辛': 4.7, '壬': 3.8, '癸': 2.7,
}
